    "name": "Spell Effect: Junk Form",
    "system": {
        "description": {
            "value": "<p>Granted by @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.Item.Junk Form]</p>\n<p>You transform into the chosen junk battle form and gain the tech trait. You can Dismiss the spell. Armor check penalties and Speed penalties are ignored. Armor upgrades and environmental protections keep working. Strikes from this form are the only attacks you can use. You are trained with them. They are Strength based, and you can use your own unarmed attack modifier if it is higher.</p>\n<p><strong>E-Waste</strong> Speed 25 feet (hover) and fly 20 feet. Hover is not a separate Speed. Weakness bludgeoning 5. Resistance electricity 10.</p>\n<p><strong>Static Feedback</strong> (electricity) A creature that hits you with a melee Strike takes 1d4 electricity damage (2d4 if this effect is 8th rank or higher). If the weapon has the tech trait, they must succeed at a Reflex save against your spell DC or the weapon becomes glitching 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Filth</strong> Speed 20 feet. Weakness slashing 5. Resistance poison 10.</p>\n<p><strong>Rancid Stench</strong> (aura, olfactory, poison) 10 feet. A creature that enters or starts its turn in the aura must succeed at a Fortitude save against your spell DC or become sickened 1 (sickened 2 on a critical failure). Creatures can't retch to reduce their sickened value within the aura. If a creature succeeds, or once they recover from this sickened condition, it is temporarily immune to the aura for 24 hours.</p>\n<p><strong>Scrap</strong> Speed 20 feet and climb 20 feet. Weakness electricity 5. Resistance slashing 10.</p>\n<p><strong>Heightened (8th)</strong> Your battle form is Huge, you gain a +15-foot status bonus to your Speeds, and your melee Strikes have 10-foot reach. AC is 21 + your level, you gain 15 temporary Hit Points, your attack modifier is +28, and your damage bonus is +12. Strike damage dice do not increase.</p>"
        },
